  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="section-faq-hero">
    <h1 class="section-heading" id="section-faq-hero">Questions, Answered</h1>
    <p class="section-sub">New to improv, or just want to know what you're walking into? Here's the honest version, first the things everyone asks before their first time, then the specifics for our regular events.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section faq-section" aria-labelledby="section-faq-first">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="section-faq-first">First Time With Us?</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">However you're coming in, watching a show, playing in a jam, or just curious, here's what to expect. Short answer to all of it: you'll be fine, and you're welcome here.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What is improv, anyway?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Theatre made up on the spot, no script. If you've seen <em>Whose Line Is It Anyway?</em> or <em>Game Changer</em> by Dropout, that's the American, comedy-first end of it: short-form, gag-a-minute, chasing the laugh. We take a more story and theatre-driven route: scenes and characters that build on each other into something with real heart, and the comedy comes naturally out of that rather than being the point. That's where the <em>lore</em> in Improvlore comes from, the stories we spin up together and never tell the same way twice.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What even is an improv show?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Live theatre with no script. We build the whole show in the moment, from your suggestions, then never do it again. Nobody, us included, knows exactly what's about to happen. We run a handful of different formats, each its own kind of show, all improvised on the spot, just structured differently. Browse them in the <a href="/library/">library</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What's a jam, and can I play even if I've never done improv?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A jam is our open, beginner-friendly session where you get to play, not just watch. And yes, that's exactly who it's for: most people who come to a jam have never been on a stage. We guide you through everything step by step, and you don't need any preparation, experience, or special skills. Bring your stage fright with you; you'll be in good company.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What's a workshop?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A deeper, more hands-on take on improv, run over 9 to 12 hours. You learn by doing, at a pace that's kind to first-timers, in a guided room where it's safe to try. Start with Improv 101 if you're new, then go as deep as you like. See what we offer in the <a href="/library/">library</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Why should I come to a show?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No two improv shows are ever the same. Whatever you see happens once and is gone, built live from the room you're in that night. You're also supporting live theatre and the people making it up in front of you. Whether it soars or it wobbles, you'll have watched something that existed for one evening only, and you helped make it.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Do I have to get on stage or perform?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Only if you want to. Taking part is always optional. At a show you can simply sit back and watch; if we ever invite suggestions or volunteers, you're free to pass and no one will single you out. Our jams (like Make Friends with the Stage) are all about playing on stage, but even there you're guided in gently and never pushed.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Will it be funny? Will it be any good?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Often very. Sometimes a scene falls apart, and honestly that's part of the fun, you're watching people catch something out of thin air without a net. That risk is the whole appeal: when it lands, it lands like nothing scripted can.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Can I come on my own?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Absolutely, plenty of people do. A lot of folks come alone and leave having made friends. Meeting new people is half the fun of it, and the room is a warm one.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What does it cost?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>It depends on the event, jams, shows, and workshops are priced differently. The price is always listed on each event, so you'll know before you book. <a href="/events/">See what's coming up →</a></p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Do I need a ticket, or can I just show up?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>All our events are ticketed. Walk-ins are usually possible, but we do sell out, so we'd really recommend booking ahead, it secures your spot, and it helps us gauge interest and plan the night. <a href="/events/">Grab a ticket →</a></p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What if I can't make it after booking?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Tickets can't be reused for another date, but they're easy to pass on: sell or give yours to a friend, or <a href="/contact/">let us know</a> and if we have walk-ins on the night we can try to sell it for you. For the full policy, see our <a href="/refunds/">refunds page</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What should I wear, and how long will it run?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Comfortable clothes you can move in. Our jams and sessions run around two hours. Each event page lists the exact start time and any specifics.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Where are you, and how do I get there?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Our home is <a href="https://underline.center" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Underline Center</a> in Indiranagar, where we've been the resident improv act since they opened. We also play other rooms around the city now and then, so always check the venue on the specific event. Each event page has a map link, and most of our venues have drinking water, restrooms, and street parking nearby.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Is it family-friendly?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>We aim to keep our shows and jams broadly PG-13 and family-friendly. Improv is live and unscripted, so the odd adult theme or bit of strong language can come up, but that's the spirit we play in. For events open to children we keep things firmly child-appropriate. If you'd like to check whether a particular event suits who you're bringing, just <a href="/contact/">ask us</a>. See our <a href="/code-of-conduct/">Code of Conduct</a> for more.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Is there alcohol or food?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No alcohol. Food and beverages are sometimes available, but it depends on the event and venue, so check the specific event if that matters to you.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What about phones?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>We ask everyone to keep phones away, at shows, jams, and workshops alike, so we can all be fully present with one another. It's a big part of what makes the room feel alive.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">I have an access need. Can you help?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Yes, we want our events to be as welcoming and accessible as possible. If you have any access needs, seating, mobility, sensory, or anything else, <a href="/contact/">let us know in advance</a> and we'll do our best to accommodate you.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How can I support Improvlore?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>The best way is simple: come to a show or a jam, and bring a friend. Showing up is what keeps live improv alive. If you're a brand or company interested in sponsoring or partnering with us, we'd love to hear from you, <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section faq-section" aria-labelledby="section-faq-sst">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="section-faq-sst">The Silliest Show Tonight</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Our weekly experimental show. Every Friday, 9 PM, at Underline Center, a brand-new unscripted show built around a director's concept and your suggestions.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What is this?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A weekly experimental unscripted improv show. Every Friday, 9 PM.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What's experimental about it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Each week a director comes in with a concept. Could be a "format", a theme, some idea they've been chewing on. We improvise the whole show around it.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">So you don't know what's going to happen?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Honestly, no. We find out alongside you.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Do I get to participate?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>You are the audience, and even though we come in with a "format", the show is built on your suggestions and prompts. A lot of the games need audience up on stage too. (If you're looking for more, come to our jams.)</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Why should I come?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>All our shows are different, no two are ever the same, and this one especially. You're also supporting live theatre and the people making it up in front of you. Whether it lands or falls apart, you'll have seen something that happened once.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">When and where?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Fridays, 9 PM. Underline Center, Indiranagar.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section faq-section" aria-labelledby="section-faq-ww">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="section-faq-ww">Whimsical Wednesday</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Our jam. An after-work hang of improv games and exercises, no stage, no audience, no performance.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What is it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>An after-work hang where people come together to play improv games and exercises in pairs and groups. Expect playful activities around storytelling, spontaneity, creativity, and connection.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Who is it for?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Anyone who enjoys playful experiences, meeting new people, and exploring creativity. No theatre, improv, or performance experience required.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Why come?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Every session has a different theme, so you'll always encounter new games, ideas, and ways to play. Even when an exercise returns, the people, stories, and discoveries are never the same, because everything is created in the moment.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Good to know</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <ul class="faq-points">
            <li>There is no stage, no audience, and no performance. This is a play-fun-games-only session. Bring your stage fright with you!</li>
            <li>These sessions are beginner-friendly, and we'll guide you through everything step by step.</li>
            <li>We encourage everyone to keep their phones away during the session so we can be fully present with one another.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Specifics</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <ul class="faq-points">
            <li>Approximately 2 hours of guided activities and games.</li>
            <li>Comfortable clothes are recommended. The venue has drinking water and restrooms, and is in proximity to residential areas, so street parking may be available.</li>
            <li>No preparation, experience, or special skills required.</li>
            <li>Plenty of laughter, surprises, and opportunities to connect with new people.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section faq-section" aria-labelledby="section-faq-mfs">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="section-faq-mfs">Make Friends with the Stage</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Our open-stage jam. Unscripted scenes, guided by our directors and cast, in a supportive room with no external audience.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What is it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>An after-work hang where people come together to explore improvisation on stage. Our directors and experienced cast members guide the scenes, helping you build confidence, spontaneity, and storytelling instincts in a supportive environment.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Who is it for?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Anyone curious about performing unscripted scenes, trying improv for the first time, or hoping to become more comfortable on stage.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Why come?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Each session presents different scene types, scenarios, characters, and prompts to play with, all of it unscripted, and made up on the spot. Each scene is unique, and each Make Friends with the Stage session is unique. Come once, or come for every session, it'll be different each time.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Good to know</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <ul class="faq-points">
            <li>There is no external audience. Participants perform for and support one another.</li>
            <li>These sessions are beginner-friendly, and you'll be guided throughout the experience.</li>
            <li>Everyone gets opportunities to perform in different scene types and group combinations.</li>
            <li>We encourage everyone to keep their phones away during the session so we can be fully present with one another.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Specifics</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <ul class="faq-points">
            <li>Approximately 2 hours of guided stage time and scene work.</li>
            <li>Comfortable clothes are recommended. The venue has drinking water and restrooms, and is in proximity to residential areas, so street parking may be available.</li>
            <li>No preparation or memorisation required.</li>
            <li>Equal parts learning, experimentation, and play.</li>
            <li>A supportive room full of people cheering each other on.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

